body: |-
  ## Why
  Field report: Kevin (deal-oracle) updated paradigm globally but his Claude still showed only 26 agents. Root-cause investigation found: `paradigm agent list` counts .agent FILES in ~/.paradigm/agents/, npm update never touches that dir (no postinstall, only `agent create --global` writes one at a time), and there was NO bundled canonical set — agents existed ad-hoc in home dirs only. So a global update could never change a user's agent count by design. Separately, the framework had three disagreeing sources of truth (CORE_AGENT_IDS=8, ROLE_PROMPTS=5 real, AGENT_TIERS=51) and the prompt assembler only injected the one-line `role`, so ~62 archetypes rendered as generic builder.

  ## What shipped
  - Bundled all 67 archetypes at packages/paradigm/templates/agents/ (ships via package `files` field, no build step).
  - `paradigm agent sync-global`: copies bundle → ~/.paradigm/agents/, skip-if-exists default (never destroys customizations), --force, --dry-run.
  - Assembler precedence fixed: ROLE_PROMPTS[name] (core 5 battle-tested constants win) → agent.description (rich persona for the other 62) → agent.role → builder. Verified end-to-end: designer→425-char description, architect→hardcoded constant.
  - AGENT_TIERS + DEFAULT_MODELS cover all 67 + deterministic tier-2/sonnet fallback at all read sites.
  - 8 thin stubs authored to canonical bar by Loid (forge): agent-evaluator/Crucible, data-model/Lattice, domain/Lexicon, regulatory/Codex, geo/Carto, offline/Tide, forms/Quill, report-gen/Press — generalized from project-specific stubs.
  - Nickname collision resolved: mobile renamed Swift→Dash; swift keeps Swift. All 67 nicknames unique.

  ## Process notes
  - Curation gate (advisor): did NOT bundle all 67 verbatim without user sign-off; presented A/B/C buckets; user chose "fix all 67 and ship."
  - The assembler change was nearly a silent no-op — agents.yaml carries `role` not `description`; verified the orchestration execute path loads .agent profiles via loadAgentProfile and plumbs description through before declaring done.
  - Behavior change flagged in CHANGELOG: custom role: overrides for the core 5 no longer win over hardcoded prompts.
